DBOS's words and this store's
Two panels. The upper one holds the two words that mean different things in
the two vocabularies — "step" and "workflow" — each shown as one word over two
meanings rather than as a mapping, because a mapping is what the panel exists
to deny: in DBOS a step is a checkpointed unit inside a workflow, and here it
is a declared unit of work a participant performs. The lower panel is the rest
of the vocabulary, each DBOS name paired by an arrow with what it is called
here: queue, partition key, executor, client, system database, send and
receive, events, listen queues, migration and workflow id. Beneath both, the
names that have no counterpart in either direction.
